INT. AGING CAVE - ALPINE CHEESE DAIRY - NIGHT

A hand-hewn tunnel, damp and cold. Shelves of wheels stacked to the ceiling, each the size of a tire, smelling of mold and old milk. Strings of bare bulbs. Water drips in a slow metronome.

Three figures in white coats and hairnets creep between the racks.

ANGELIKA STROBL, 40s, lean, planner, carries a thermal scanner. DIETMAR "DIDI" HOFER, 50s, safecracker, wears a headlamp and a toolbelt. PETRA LUNDQVIST-AGYEMAN, 30s, driver, clutches a walkie. And the night watchman, FRAU BERGMANN, 60s, somewhere above them, a flashlight in her fist and a radio on her hip, who has not yet noticed anything.

A bulb flickers.

ANGELIKA
(whispering)
Aisle nine. Wheel forty.

DIDI
Which wheel?

ANGELIKA
The one with the red seal.

They fan out. Didi knocks a wheel. It rocks. Petra lunges. Catches it. Her biceps shake.

PETRA
(through teeth)
Careful.

DIDI
Sorry.

Angelika finds it. A wheel the size of a wagon, wax-sealed. She taps. It rings hollow.

ANGELIKA
Didi.

He kneels. Cracks the seal with a pick. Wax flakes. Inside: a steel box.

DIDI
Hello, beautiful.

PETRA
It's in the cheese?

ANGELIKA
Forty years. Nobody looks in a wheel.

Didi lifts the box. A click. A light.

A flashlight beam sweeps the aisle above.

BERGMANN (O.S.)
(sharp)
Wer ist da?

Everyone freezes. Petra mouths a curse.

ANGELIKA
(whispering)
Night watch.

The beam comes closer. Footsteps on the gantry. A shadow spills between the racks.

Didi bolts. Slams into a shelf. Wheels tumble. A cascade of cheese thunders down the aisle.

He drops the box. Petra yanks him back. Angelika snatches it mid-air, ducks, rolls through the wreckage.

BERGMANN (O.S.) (CONT'D)
Halt!

They scramble. Cheese everywhere. The beam sweeps wildly.

PETRA
Go go go!

All three bolt for the tunnel mouth, slipping on rinds. Behind them, a landslide of Gruyere pours into the aisle and buries the guard to her ankles.

EXT. CAVE MOUTH - NIGHT

A van idles. They pile in. Petra floors it. The van lurches down the mountain road.

INT. VAN - CONTINUOUS

Angelika opens the steel box. Inside: a single wheel of cheese, tiny, perfect, no bigger than a palm. She stares.

DIDI
That's it?

ANGELIKA
(wonder)
The Madame Esterhazy. Eighty thousand euros a pound.

DIDI
It smells like feet.

PETRA
(grinning)
Smells like retirement.
